    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "The change is complete and the full test suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`, Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0).\n\n## Summary\n\nI moved date-derived values to a fiscal-year basis (fiscal year starts 1 July, named after the calendar year it ends in, so `2026-08-10` \u2192 **FY27**).\n\n**New util** \u2014 `util/FiscalYear.java`:\n- `of(date)` \u2014 fiscal year number (calendar year, +1 from July onward).\n- `label(date)` \u2014 `FY<YY>` format.\n- `elapsed(from, to)` \u2014 whole fiscal years crossed (1-July boundaries).\n\n**`fiscalYear` field (new)**:\n- Added the `fiscalYear` property to `openapi.yml` (generates the DTO getter/setter).\n- Mapped it in `OwnerMapper` as `FiscalYear.label(owner.getRegistrationDate())`. The registration date is already business-day-adjusted in `BuildOwner`, satisfying \"derived from the business-day-adjusted registration date.\"\n\n**Membership identifier year segment** \u2014 now the fiscal year instead of the calendar year:\n- `OwnerMapper.membershipNumber` and `AuditOwnerCreated` now use `FiscalYear.of(...) % 100` (e.g. `NSW-...-M27` in the audit log).\n\n**Tenure** \u2014 now elapsed fiscal years instead of a 365-day window:\n- `MembershipLevel.points` awards +3 when `FiscalYear.elapsed(registrationDate, today) > 1` (was `ChronoUnit.DAYS.between(...) > 365`).\n\nI also updated the OpenAPI descriptions for `membershipNumber` and `membershipPoints`, and the Javadoc on `MembershipLevel`, to match the new fiscal-year behaviour.\n\nOne interpretation worth flagging: the spec says \"tenure counted in elapsed fiscal years rather than 365-day windows\" but doesn't pin the exact threshold. I mapped the original \"over 365 days\" (more than one year) to \"more than one elapsed fiscal year\" (`> 1`), preserving the \"substantial tenure\" gate. If you intended `>= 1` (any fiscal-year boundary crossed), that's a one-character change.",
